  "deferred": [
    {
      "source_id": "postfit/POSTFIT-SURFACE-extract_Gamma",
      "reason": "Julia surface extract_Gamma already exists (src/extract_gamma.jl, exported) and is independently tested (test/test_coevolution_*.jl), so this is NOT a missing-Julia-surface case. No proven R-parity fixture for a coevolution (fit_coevolution_gaussian-class) model exists anywhere in this repo's tools/ or test/parity/ (grep -rl fit_coevolution_gaussian test/*.jl test/parity/*.jl returns only pure-Julia test files, zero RCall/gllvmTMB coevolution fixtures). Constructing one from scratch (correct R make_cross_kernel-style formula + tree + kernel spec) without live R access to verify is out of scope for this batch; would need a follow-up slice with its own proven fixture."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "postfit/POSTFIT-SURFACE-extract_lv_effects",
      "reason": "Julia surface exists (src/postfit.jl extract_lv_effects(fit::GllvmFit; type)) but requires a fit built with fit_gaussian_gllvm(...; X_lv=...) (a constrained-ordination predictor block) -- the gaussian_small fixture this batch reuses has no X_lv term, so extract_lv_effects(fit_g) would throw ArgumentError on the very fixture the rest of this batch shares. Pairing it against R's own X_lv-analogous route needs a distinct fixture; out of scope for this batch, flagged for a follow-up slice."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "postfit/POSTFIT-SURFACE-extract_phylo_signal",
      "reason": "Julia surface exists (src/extractors.jl forwards to phylo_signal(fit::GllvmFit; \u03a3_phy)), but GLLVM.jl's route takes an externally-supplied \u03a3_phy on an ordinary GllvmFit while R's extract_phylo_signal() reads report$Sigma_phy off a genuine phylo_latent()/phylo_indep() structured fit -- the two are not the same model class. A numerically paired comparison needs a live R phylo formula fit on the SAME tree/Y as the Julia \u03a3_phy, which cannot be safely constructed and verified without R access in this session."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "namespace/export/profile_ci_phylo_signal",
      "reason": "Same phylo model-class mismatch as extract_phylo_signal above; profile_ci_phylo_signal additionally needs a working bracket-then-bisect profile over that same R phylo fit."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "postfit/POSTFIT-SURFACE-profile_ci_phylo_signal",
      "reason": "Same as namespace/export/profile_ci_phylo_signal (duplicate ledger row, same underlying surface)."
    },
    {
      "source_id": "namespace/export/slope_sd_ci",
      "reason": "Julia surface exists (src/confint_derived_wald.jl, slope_sd_ci on GaussianRandomSlopeFit), but the R oracle route (.unlazy/core070-aghq/oracle-source/readback/R/slope-sd-ci.R) is explicitly documented in its own header as having a prior hand-indexing failure mode ('a first attempt at the phylo route indexed theta_dep_chol entries 2/5/8 instead of the correct 2/4/6') and needs an ADREPORT-differentiated packed expression read off sd_report -- the exact R formula/grouping-factor grammar for the diagonal augmented-slope route (theta_diag_B_slope) that would pair with GLLVM.jl's per-group \u03a3_b random-slope fit is not something this batch could construct and verify without live R access."
    },
    {
